```

The issue is that `ap_int.h` is not available in the plain C++ compilation environment used for checking. Since the wide-bus approach requires HLS-specific headers that aren't available at compile-check time, the smallest fix is to revert to using the original `double*` pointer signatures (which the header already declares) and implement memory coalescing through burst-friendly access patterns with the existing pragmas, rather than using `ap_uint<512>`. This keeps the code compilable while preserving all other optimizations.

